&lt;p&gt;At Squarespace, we believe great talent experiences help people do their best work. We&#39;re looking for a Principal Talent Management Partner to help shape how we support performance, growth, careers, and development across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a builder role with end-to-end ownership of our Talent Management portfolio, including performance management, talent reviews, succession planning, career development, internal mobility, skills, and future talent initiatives. You&#39;ll connect these programs into simple, scalable experiences that help employees grow, managers lead effectively, and the business make better talent decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working closely with People Business Partners, leaders, and cross-functional teams, you&#39;ll turn strategy into action - designing and delivering programs, facilitating critical talent conversations, using data to improve our approach, and leveraging AI and technology to modernize how talent experiences are delivered.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for someone who thrives in ambiguity, brings structure to complex ideas, and is equally energized by shaping strategy and making it happen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own and evolve our talent experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and continuously evolve Squarespace&#39;s Talent Management portfolio across performance, talent reviews, succession, careers, internal mobility, skills, and emerging talent priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design connected, scalable experiences that support employee growth, manager effectiveness, and business performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring fresh thinking and practical ideas to how we develop talent and prepare for the future of work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape the future of performance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve performance management toward a continuous experience centered on feedback, coaching, accountability, and development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design experiences that fit naturally into the flow of work and make meaningful feedback part of everyday conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create practical frameworks, resources, and tools that help managers lead performance and career conversations with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use workforce insights, employee feedback, and program metrics to proactively identify opportunities, measure impact, and continuously improve the talent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead strategy through execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex initiatives from strategy and design through implementation, adoption, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage roadmaps, project plans, stakeholder alignment, governance, and delivery across multiple priorities and programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive change that is thoughtful, practical, and easy for employees and managers to adopt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner, communicate, and influence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted Talent Management partner to People Business Partners, leaders, and cross-functional stakeholders, providing expertise, guidance, and practical recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships and influence through expertise, collaboration, thoughtful recommendations, and data-informed insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop clear communications, presentations, toolkits, and enablement resources that help employees and managers understand, adopt, and get value from our talent programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex talent concepts and data into clear, compelling, and actionable insights tailored for different audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build with AI &amp;amp; Emerging Technology&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and experiment with AI tools, workflows, and automations to solve talent problems, simplify processes, and create better experiences for employees and managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify where AI can strengthen talent practices - from skills and internal mobility to talent insights and manager enablement and turn promising ideas into practical solutions that can scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply sound judgment about where and how to use AI, balancing innovation with quality, privacy, bias, employee experience, and the importance of human judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who You Are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of progressive experience in Talent Management, Talent Development, Organizational Development, or a related People discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating at both strategic and tactical levels - connecting Talent Management priorities to business objectives, shaping functional strategy and direction, and driving hands-on execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced leading complex, cross-functional programs from concept through implementation and adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong program manager who brings structure, clarity, and momentum to ambiguous and complex problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An effective communicator and facilitator who can influence stakeholders at multiple levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled at building trusted partnerships across functions and is sought out for expertise, sound judgment, and practical recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using data and insights to identify opportunities, measure impact, and inform decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced building or experimenting with AI tools, workflows, or automations to solve people or business problems, with strong judgment about where AI can create value and where human judgment matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identifies opportunities to improve programs, processes, and ways of working with a focus on scalable, sustainable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about creating simple, intuitive talent experiences that help employees grow and managers succeed, balancing strategic thinking with hands-on execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Squarespace?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to shape how Talent Management works at Squarespace. You&#39;ll have the autonomy to build, experiment, and improve experiences that influence how employees grow, managers lead, and teams succeed - while helping evolve our talent practices for the future of work.&lt;/p&gt;
